WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV v3.0 — ai-reads-human (45s) Narrator Sean

1
00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:05.087
First, computers often swap data in text formats written for human eyes,

2
00:00:05.087 --> 00:00:07.558
forcing machines to spend extra work.

3
00:00:07.998 --> 00:00:12.220
Second, reading indented configuration text took over two thousand

4
00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:16.058
times more chip energy than reading compact machine numbers.

5
00:00:16.498 --> 00:00:20.542
Third, chopping structured text into AI word pieces burned

6
00:00:20.542 --> 00:00:24.308
twelve times more energy than parsing the text itself.

7
00:00:24.748 --> 00:00:31.152
Imagine two calculators mailing spelled-out paragraphs to each other instead of passing numbers directly.

8
00:00:31.152 --> 00:00:38.593
Software agents routinely turn clean memory into punctuated text, only for the next program to parse every character back.

9
00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:44.772
The practical fix is clear: let machines exchange compact binary records with other machines,

10
00:00:44.772 --> 00:00:49.092
and render friendly text only on screen when a person asks to read it.
